      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: It\u0027s cleaner and more efficient to use a `visited` set to track which nodes have been traversed, rather than modifying an `unvisited` set. This avoids having to copy the `unvisited` set before iterating, and importantly, it inherently guards against stack overflows if there happens to be a cycle in the dependency graph (since `visited.insert(n)` happens *before* recursing, whereas `unvisited.erase(n)` happens *after* recursing).\n\n```cpp\n  std::unordered_set\u003cconst Target*\u003e visited;\n  std::vector\u003cTarget*\u003e targets;\n  \n  std::function\u003cvoid(Target*)\u003e visit \u003d [\u0026](Target* n) {\n    if (!visited.insert(n).second)\n      return;\n\n    for (const auto\u0026 pair : n-\u003eGetDeps(Target::DEPS_LINKED)) {\n      visit(const_cast\u003cTarget*\u003e(pair.ptr));\n    }\n\n    targets.push_back(n);\n  };\n\n  for (auto\u0026 record : records_) {\n    if (record.type() \u003d\u003d BuilderRecord::ITEM_TARGET \u0026\u0026 record.item()) {\n      visit(record.item()-\u003eAsTarget());\n    }\n  }\n```",
